DOCX export filter
==================

This filter converts an ODT package to a WordprocessingML DOCX package. It
traverses the ODT content with OdtReader and OdfTextReader backends, writes the
document and style XML, collects package parts in DocxFile, and emits OPC
relationship parts and [Content_Types].xml when creating the final package.

The current exporter supports a limited subset of DOCX. It writes basic text,
simple tables, comments, hyperlinks, explicit spaces and line breaks, and maps
a subset of paragraph and character formatting. It does not yet provide full
fidelity for merged or styled tables, lists, images, page sections, headers and
footers, fields, or many advanced Word features. Unsupported ODF constructs
may be lost in conversion.

Key classes
-----------

DocxExport                  Coordinates ODT traversal and DOCX package output
OdfReaderDocxContext        Holds output XML writers and the package collector
OdfTextReaderDocxBackend    Converts ODF paragraphs, runs, links, and comments
DocxStyleWriter             Writes Word style definitions
DocxStyleHelper             Maps supported ODF text and paragraph properties
DocxFile                    Collects package parts and writes the DOCX package
OpcRelSet                   Stores and serializes relationships for one part
OpcRelSetManager            Writes package-level and part-level relationships

Relationship sets are generated from the relationships registered during the
conversion. Add relationships through DocxFile::addRelationship so that the
relationship identifiers used in document XML match the emitted .rels parts.
